# git
.git
.gitignore
*.md
!README.md
LICENSE

# local state
.env
workspace/
*.log

# ci
.github

# Not build inputs — verified with grep: no COPY (and no build-time script the
# Dockerfile runs) reads anything under these paths, so excluding them only
# trims the context.
tests/
research/
__pycache__/
.td-wf/
win32_mcp_shots/

# `docs/` is deliberately NOT excluded. The brief expected it to be droppable,
# but the Dockerfile COPYs `docs/windows-iso-sources.md` into the in-image
# cua-check tree (and a flat-tree assertion in tools/check-cua-vm.mjs fails the
# build if it does not land as `windows-iso-sources.md`), so excluding the
# directory would break `docker build`. The long-form notes under it are already
# outside the context when they sit at the root (`*.md` above); as `docs/*.md`
# they are now included, ~360 KB of markdown that no COPY reads. Left in place
# rather than pattern-matched, because a second don't-ship-this exception list
# is exactly how the next COPY breaks silently.
